1
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:09,500
Before the glass broke, we had only one rule out here on the pillars:

2
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,000
Tend the oil.

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:20,300
Watch the mist, and never, ever look into the water at night.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:32,800
Because lanterns are heavy things, and yet tonight, every flame is leaning up toward the dark.

5
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,000
Stars are not supposed to blink.

6
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:47,400
Stars are not supposed to fall slowly, and they are certainly not supposed to weep.

7
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:55,000
The old hydraulics groan. The optic shifts to red.

8
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,000
It is time to throw.

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,800
A net of light is not cast to catch.

10
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,000
It is woven to cradle.

11
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:23,500
Three hundred fathoms of spun copper, resting on a tide that has no bottom.

12
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:33,000
When your palm touches the ember, you feel two hearts beating out of time.

13
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:37,200
And it knows your name.

14
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:50,000
The tide stops breathing.

15
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:54,500
The horizon folds down its eyes.

16
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,500
Sixteen hundred meters of sky...

17
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:01,200
...coming down to claim its blood.

18
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,200
Look at the lanterns on the pillars.

19
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:11,500
Look at how they pulse.

20
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:20,000
They were never lanterns. They were beacons.

21
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:30,000
The sea stands upright like a wall.

22
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:33,800
The sky becomes the deck.

23
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:39,500
Every angle we trusted is coming undone.

24
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,500
The spinning top hums against the iron plate, wobbly...

25
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:50,000
...but never falling.

26
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:55,500
Whose dream are we drowning in?

27
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:10,500
There is only one way up.

28
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:13,500
Up the spiral. Listen to the pulse.

29
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:18,500
One tick is one winter.

30
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:25,500
Another tick, a decade gone.

31
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:32,500
The wall of water stands frozen behind.

32
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:38,000
The sky tears open like rice paper.

33
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:42,000
And behind the stars...

34
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,500
...there is light.

35
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,800
A room with no corners.

36
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,000
Stone that swallows all shadows.

37
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:01,500
Inside the glass...

38
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:05,000
...no man.

39
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,000
Waiting to be emptied.

40
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:16,000
The little one has no wings left.

41
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:22,000
It will never reach the high dark on cold embers.

42
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,000
Take it.

43
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:31,000
It was only borrowed, anyway.

44
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:37,500
You remember now.

45
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,800
The water is mirror-smooth again.

46
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:48,000
Looking up through the depths...

47
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:55,000
...you finally see it.

48
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
The stars were never above.
